<body lang=3D"ZH-TW" link=3D"blue" vlink=3D"purple" style=3D"text-justify-t=
rim:punctuation">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Hi there,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I was trying to add some pre-bu=
ilt binaries and files by using a recipe.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">The recipe has something like t=
his:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">SRC_URI =3D <a href=3D"file:///=
\\files">file://files</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">=A1K<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">do_install() {<o:p></o:p></span=
></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; install =A1V=
d ${D}<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">}<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">FILES_${PN} =3D =A1=A7/*=A1=A8<=
o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">ALLOW_EMPTY_${PN} =3D =A1=A71=
=A1=A8<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">INSANE_SKIP_${PN} =3D =A1=A7deb=
ug-files dev-so=A1=A8<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">The result was all the binaries=
 and files installed and packages are created,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">But I also found kernel header =
files are also built in under /usr/include in rootfs image.<o:p></o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">For my understanding those head=
er files should be used if I want to develop/debug applications on the targ=
et device but it is not the case.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Also I noticed the use of INSAN=
E_SKIP_${PN} so I check the usage of debug-files and dev-so,<o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">And it turned out there are .de=
bug folders in the WORKDIR/package folder so I thought that is why debug-fi=
les was used.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">The questions are,<o:p></o:p></=
span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Why are those kernel header fil=
es installed in rootfs? How do I prevent this?<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Why are there .debug in the pac=
kage folder, it should only be in package =A1Vdbg folder, right?<o:p></o:p>=
</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">I searched and figured maybe it=
 has something to do with the do_install task but I can=A1=A6t find a solut=
ion.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Any suggestions?<o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Thanks,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Andy<o:p></o:p></span></p>
